/* Where the exchange lands: not one name, a short list of people, each of whom
   can be opened.

   Prior experience in the same kind of matter is one ground for putting
   somebody on the list, and it is the strongest, but it is not the only one —
   who takes new matters this week, who sits in the same city as the
   counterparty, who works the neighbouring discipline the question will touch
   next. So every person carries the ground they are here on, named, and the
   list is honest about it: the first entry is the recommendation and stands
   open, the rest are folded and open on a click, into exactly the same card.

   Each card carries the person's own direct line and address. A visitor at
   22:40 who has been told who to call must be able to call them, without a
   form, a hand-off or a search on the site — and the switchboard in the rail
   stays the way out for anyone who would rather not.

   The reason line is retrieved from the mandate record, so it is quoted rather
   than asserted. Without a source there is no reason line: the suppressed
   state says so plainly instead of paraphrasing. */

