/* The rail: the right-hand region of the conversation drawer.

   Two things live in it and nothing else. At the top, permanently, how to
   reach the firm without any of this — the switchboard, the four offices, the
   hours. It does not scroll away, recede or collapse as the exchange gets
   better, because a visitor who decides three turns in that this is not
   working has to be able to leave by telephone without scrolling anywhere.
   That also settles the cold state: at turn zero the rail holds the contact
   details and nothing else, and that is a finished state — nothing is phrased
   as though something were pending.

   Below it, in chapters, what this conversation has turned up: links into
   Vinge's own site, and people. One chapter per machine turn, so every item
   is bound to the turn that produced it. Links carry an arrow and a rule and
   sit under a chapter heading — the failure mode designed against is a rail
   that reads as a summary panel, which nobody clicks. A person carries one
   line saying why they are on the list, and that line is retrieved, not
   written: a fact from the mandate record with its source under it. Without a
   source there is no reason line.

   The rail re-specifies rather than only growing. An item that a later,
   sharper item replaces is marked superseded: it stays in its own chapter,
   reachable, but it is not part of what the rail is currently saying. By the
   last turn the rail is shorter and sharper than it was in the middle.

   Reading position. Scrolling the transcript back to an earlier turn brings
   that turn's items back. Two ways to show it, and the mode says which:
   `swap` shows the chapter being read on its own, `expand` shows every chapter
   with the one being read emphasised. Either way, getting back to the newest
   state is one move — the return line at the top of the chapters, which is
   only there while the visitor is somewhere else. */

